      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you mean about preserving the universal aspect of art. But some people argue that the very idea of \"universal human experience\" is just a way to protect the status quo and ignore how power dynamics shape what we consider \"beautiful.\" They'd say that \"aesthetic beauty\" is often just a standard set by a specific group of people. In that light, wouldn't focusing on political messaging actually be a way to make art more honest and inclusive?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
